      <h2 id="how-we-evaluated">How We Evaluated</h2>
      <p>We evaluated each tool on how well it performs the four core SEO jobs in a realistic weekly workflow: running a site audit and acting on it, researching and clustering keywords, tracking rankings over time, and optimizing a draft against live SERPs. We drew on vendor documentation, published feature sets, and community consensus from SEO practitioners and agency teams, following the <a href="/how-we-test/">ToolStep review protocol</a>. Pricing is listed as "from" because most vendors tier by usage — always confirm current pricing on the vendor's site before buying.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Audit depth &amp; issue prioritization (30%)</strong> — crawl coverage, the number and relevance of technical checks, and whether the tool tells you what to fix first instead of dumping 400 warnings on you</li>
        <li><strong>Keyword research quality (25%)</strong> — database size, long-tail expansion, difficulty scoring accuracy, intent classification, and clustering</li>
        <li><strong>Rank tracking &amp; monitoring (20%)</strong> — refresh frequency, location/device granularity, volatility alerts, and trend reporting</li>
        <li><strong>Content optimization (15%)</strong> — SERP benchmarking, topic term suggestions, and content scoring</li>
        <li><strong>Workflow &amp; pricing (10%)</strong> — how much of the above lives in one place without repeated exports, and cost for an independent site or small team</li>
      </ul>

